163	\paragraph{Base vs.\ Instruct.} Both Qwen2.5-1.5B base and instruct variants yield $K^*=2$ (AUC 1v2: 0.682 vs.\ 0.696). The instruct model shows lower vocabulary diversity at gen-1 (0.54 vs.\ 0.58; KS test $p=0.01$), suggesting that alignment training acts as a mild form of mode collapse, but this does not affect the saturation boundary.
164	
165	\paragraph{Cross-Scale Probe.} Qwen2.5-7B yields AUC 2v3 = 0.612 averaged across three seeds, with individual seeds producing $K^*$ values of 2, 3, and 2 (majority: 2). This provides suggestive but inconclusive evidence that $K^*$ may increase with model scale; the effect is within seed variance at our sample size (1K documents). Ordinal accuracy improves to 0.44 (vs.\ 0.42 for 1.5B), consistent with the larger model's richer channel preserving more distinguishable structure.
166	
